    "problem_statement": "During Thread-over-BLE (TCAT) commissioning, the secure-connection state callback is invoked more than once when a locally-initiated BLE disconnect is requested, even though only a single disconnect should be reported. Additionally, when the advertising data is expected to change after a connection is torn down (for example because a partial dataset now affects the advertised flag), the advertisement data is not refreshed and is not retained, so observers see no change or an unset advertisement. The connection-state callback must be reported exactly once per connection/disconnect transition, and the advertisement data must be updated (and persisted for the next advertising phase) when it is expected to change, including when the device is not currently in the active advertising state.",
